                <pb facs="0524" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.3715/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Valencia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-10T16:00:00-04:30">June 10, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 11—12:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>668. My X–527, March 4, 1 p.m. Cuban Embassy inquires whether we can have a naval
                    vessel at Alicante June 16th to evacuate about 120 Cubans, three-fourths of whom
                    are expected to be women and children.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
